@flexiarg institutions/monitoring-the-resource
@title Monitoring The Resource
@keywords monitoring, resource condition, accountability, Ostrom 4B, common-pool resources
@audience institution designers, commons researchers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Ostrom design principle 4B, wording as in Cox, Arnold and Tomas (2010), "A review of design principles for community-based natural resource management", Ecology and Society 15(4):38, quoted in Corneli 2016 (ICCC 2016) Table 1. Original source Ostrom 1990, Governing the Commons. Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29.
@status draft 2026-10-29; to vet against Ostrom 1990 and Cox et al. 2010 before relying on non-quoted text
@references [institutions/ARGUMENT creativity-commons/producers-can-modify-the-tests]

! conclusion:
  "Monitors who are accountable to the users monitor the condition of the resource."

  + context:
    Monitoring of the resource's state, as distinct from users' behaviour.

  + IF:
    The resource can degrade even when every user follows the rules.

  + HOWEVER:
    Resource condition can be hard and costly to measure, and indicators can mislead.

  + THEN:
    Assign monitoring of the resource's condition to people accountable to the users, and feed the findings into rule revision.

  + BECAUSE:
    Rules are only as good as the users' knowledge of the resource; condition data shows when the rules need to change.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Vet the HOWEVER and BECAUSE against Ostrom 1990 and Cox et al. 2010; only the conclusion is quoted.]
    next[Creativity-commons transposition: creativity-commons/producers-can-modify-the-tests.]
